        <p>WAHRINOTON MUNICIPAL ELECTIONS, 1893. TO THE BURGESSES OF THE LATCHFORD WARD. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN, My term of office has now expired. After many years of continuous and active service in the Town Council a.; the representative of your Ward. I have been asked to continue that service, which I cheerfully do, as I arn and have been for some time past connected in Com- mittees with au extensive scheme of pay ng and lighting the streets and roads of Latchford, many of which are a ready done. Should I again be returned, I promise to do my hest In this 'direction, and in any other essential to your interests. Thanking you for past kindness, and trusting to the sup- port of all on the let November next. I am, Ladies and Gentlemen, Yours faithfully. JOSEPH ASHION.</p>
